cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  Please cite this project and the upstream manuscript. This is a conditional
  research draft; include the repository commit used until a release is archived.
title: "A sharper exponent for integer multiplication"
authors:
  - family-names: Colkitt
    given-names: Douglas
  - family-names: Prosz
    given-names: Aurel
license: Apache-2.0
type: software
repository-code: "https://github.com/Paureel/integer-mult-bounds"
url: "https://github.com/Paureel/integer-mult-bounds"
abstract: >-
  Exact rational certificates, source patches, and research notes for conditional
  improvements to OpenAI's integer-multiplication manuscript. Compact dirty-control
  fields remove the simultaneous layer's spacing penalty. Together with complete
  temporary reservations, local exceptional repair, a separately sized complex
  network, and retained refinements, the supplied written proofs support
  kappa = 83/10^12 > 2^-34. The complete upstream algorithmic theorem is assumed;
  the new arguments are not independently reviewed or formally verified.
keywords:
  - integer multiplication
  - computational complexity
  - exact arithmetic
  - parameter optimization
  - reproducible research
references:
  - type: software
    title: "A sharper exponent for integer multiplication (base repository)"
    authors:
